From 8c68f30431dd26247ef753e645286644183f9b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wine-thumbs <wine-thumbs@localhost>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:56:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] comdlg32: Use the item dialog for GetOpenFileName and
 GetSaveFileName.

Like Windows since Vista, calls without a hook, a template or a help
button get the item dialog; the OPENFILENAME fields are mapped to it and
the result is written back as the Explorer style dialog does, including
multiple selection, OFN_READONLY through the Open drop-down, the ANSI
variants and FNERR_BUFFERTOOSMALL. HKCU\Software\Wine\FileDialog
"Classic"=1, also per application under AppDefaults, keeps the old one.

Both dialogs also follow Windows 7 in opening the folder used last when
an application passes the lpstrInitialDir it passed the first time.
